description:
transit/peering/session.rs:257: read_dot_stuffed checks size as buf.len() + output_line.len(), where output_line is the trimmed line (stripped of 
). The check uses pre-reformat length. When the line is later re-added with 
 appended via format!(), the actual stored bytes can exceed MAX_ARTICLE_BYTES by 2 per line (LF-only input gets 
). An article sent as MAX_ARTICLE_BYTES-1 bytes of LF-terminated lines can slip through the size check. Fix: measure output_line.len() after formatting (including the 
 suffix) before adding to buf.
